.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt XARGS 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm xargs
.Nd construct argument lists and run a command
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 0rtx
.Op Fl n Ar max
.Op Fl I Ar repl
.Op Fl s Ar size
.Op Ar command Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads items from standard input, appends the items to
.Ar command
and its initial arguments, and runs the resulting command.
A command that is not specified defaults to
.Ic echo .
.Pp
By default, items are separated by blanks, tabs and newlines.
Single and double quotes group blanks into one item, and a backslash escapes the next character.
An unmatched quote or a trailing backslash is an input error.
.Pp
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl 0
Separate input items with NUL bytes instead of blanks and newlines.
.It Fl n Ar max
Use at most
.Ar max
items per command.
.It Fl I Ar repl
Replace every occurrence of
.Ar repl
in the command and its initial arguments with one input line.
This implies one item per invocation and strict size checking.
If
.Ar repl
does not occur in the command, the command runs unchanged once per item.
.It Fl r
Do not run the command when the input is empty.
Without
.Fl r ,
an empty input runs the command once with no appended items.
.It Fl t
Write each command to standard error before running it.
.It Fl x
Exit with an error if an
.Fl n
group would exceed the
.Fl s
size instead of splitting the group.
A single item larger than
.Fl s
is always an error.
.It Fl s Ar size
Limit a command line to
.Ar size
bytes.
The default bound is 4096 bytes.
.El
.Pp
The command is executed with the items appended in input order.
The child's exit status is mapped to the POSIX xargs status: 0 for success, 123 for a child exit
1-125, 124 for 255, 125 for a signal, 126 when the command cannot be invoked, and 127 when the
command is not found.
.Pp
On the target image the command is resolved in the initfs
.Pa /bin
and
.Pa /sbin
and started through the native spawn path.
Standard input items are read from the console terminal; there is no general process pipeline
handle yet.
.Pp
Only the listed options are implemented.
GNU extensions such as
.Fl L ,
.Fl P ,
.Fl o ,
.Fl e ,
.Fl d ,
.Fl a
and
.Fl p
are not supported.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Status 1 indicates an input or size error, status 2 invalid usage, and the xargs-specific child
status codes are listed above.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr patch 1 ,
.Xr rsh 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The bounded core follows the POSIX.1-2024
.Nm
model for the listed options.
